{"author":{"id":"2462ded6f56967dde059994c39a506c79e39e5dfd10c5a07f07a23a5652a8353"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1776898516,"nonce":"jArcIXiAsrYnGa0pnydXaM9rpns=","title":"Disable git-bug remote sync by default","message":"## Problem\n\nThe watcher calls `tracker.sync()` periodically, which runs `git-bug pull` + `git-bug push`. This causes:\n1. Lock contention and 30s timeouts when refs diverge\n2. Repeated \"some refs were not updated\" errors\n3. Unnecessary overhead for single-user setups\n\nRemote sync was never a formal requirement (no REQ-xxx).\n\n## Proposed Solution\n\nDisable sync by default. Add optional `tracker.sync: true` in WORKFLOW.md for users who need it.\n\n## Files\n- adapters/trackers/git_bug.py - make sync() a no-op by default\n- core/config/models.py - add sync field to TrackerConfig\n- host/watcher/host_watcher.py - respect the config\n\nREQ: None (removing undocumented behavior)","files":null}]}